1
00:00:05,780 --> 00:00:08,780
Respect the lab and respect your colleagues.
尊重实验室，也尊重你的同事。

2
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:14,780
Your behavior goes a long way to ensuring that the lab is a safe environment for everyone.
你的行为对确保实验室对每个人都是安全的环境有着重要作用。

3
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:20,780
The first consideration is to follow the written standard operating procedures, step by step.
首先要考虑的是，按照书面的标准操作规程，一步一步地操作。

4
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:25,780
Never eat, drink, chew gum, or apply makeup while in the lab.
在实验室里绝不要吃东西、喝水、嚼口香糖或化妆。

5
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:29,780
You don't want to contaminate your skin or risk ingesting poisonous chemicals.
你不希望污染自己的皮肤，或冒着误食有毒化学品的风险。

6
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:33,780
You could also contaminate your experiment and ruin the results.
你还可能污染你的实验，毁掉实验结果。

7
00:00:33,780 --> 00:00:34,780
Never work alone.
绝不要独自工作。

8
00:00:34,780 --> 00:00:40,780
Always have at least one other person in the lab so that you can help each other in case of an emergency.
实验室里始终至少要有另外一个人，这样遇到紧急情况时可以互相帮助。

9
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:42,780
Good housekeeping will prevent accidents too.
良好的整理整顿也能预防事故。

10
00:00:42,780 --> 00:00:45,780
A cluttered lab is a dangerous lab.
杂乱的实验室就是危险的实验室。

11
00:00:45,780 --> 00:00:49,780
Dispose of any trash or debris on the floor which could cause someone to fall.
清理地面上任何可能让人摔倒的垃圾或杂物。

12
00:00:49,780 --> 00:00:53,780
Never place any chemical bottles on the floor, not even temporarily.
绝不要把任何化学品瓶放在地上，哪怕是暂时的也不行。

13
00:00:53,780 --> 00:00:58,780
If you do make a spill, check the safety data sheet for the appropriate response.
如果你确实洒出了东西，请查看安全技术说明书，了解适当的应对方法。

14
00:00:58,780 --> 00:01:02,780
For a routine spill, clean it immediately and place a wet floor sign.
对于常规的泄漏，要立即清理，并放置“小心地滑”的标志。

15
00:01:02,780 --> 00:01:04,780
Keep your workbench clean and organized.
保持实验台干净整齐。

16
00:01:04,780 --> 00:01:06,780
Have only the materials you need.
只放你需要的材料。

17
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:08,780
Store away all unneeded items.
把所有不需要的物品收起来。

18
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:13,780
Don't place materials near the edge of the workbench where they can easily be knocked off.
不要把材料放在实验台边缘，那里很容易被碰落。

19
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:16,780
Never try to pick up broken glass with your bare hands.
绝不要徒手去捡碎玻璃。

20
00:01:16,780 --> 00:01:23,780
A cut or puncture caused by broken glass may introduce a hazardous chemical directly into your bloodstream.
碎玻璃造成的割伤或刺伤，可能会把危险化学品直接带入你的血液。

21
00:01:23,780 --> 00:01:27,780
Dispose the glass in a designated broken glass container.
把玻璃丢弃到指定的碎玻璃收集容器中。

22
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:30,780
After you've finished an experiment, wash and dry glassware.
完成实验后，清洗并晾干玻璃器皿。

23
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:37,780
Return reagents to the storage area and clean the workbench surface with ethanol or isopropyl alcohol.
把试剂放回储存区，并用乙醇或异丙醇擦拭实验台台面。

24
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:44,780
If a safety violation occurs or you notice any unsafe condition in the lab, report it immediately to your supervisor.
如果发生违反安全规定的情况，或者你注意到实验室里有任何不安全的状况，请立即向你的主管报告。

25
00:01:44,780 --> 00:01:46,780
Be on your best behavior.
拿出你最好的表现。

26
00:01:46,780 --> 00:01:52,780
In our next lesson, we'll look at some specific chemical hazards that are common in laboratories.
在下一课中，我们将了解实验室中常见的一些具体化学危害。
